# Release-only: drop BusyBox's wget applet from shipped images.
#
# Nothing on the device uses it — the app's add-on/feed installer fetches over
# Python's urllib.request, RAUC is handed a local bundle, and no script in this
# tree calls wget. GNU wget (GPL-3.0+) was removed from the target separately;
# this applet is GPL-2.0 and so irrelevant to the licence audit. It is removed
# purely to deny a sealed appliance a generic download primitive, which is a
# standard post-exploitation convenience.
#
# Merged only via configs/release.fragment, so dev images keep wget for bench
# work — the same dev/release split already used for SSH, the gettys and the
# serial console.
# CONFIG_WGET is not set
